   "content.0b75c1780ed2": "Test-only page. Compare the old SVG simulator, the new unified renderer (synthetic route → real openpilot math), and a real recorded modelV2 stream.",
   "content.e310ca338543": "The same synthetic route is rendered through openpilot's real calcFrameMatrix → drawModelRenderFrame pipeline.",
   "content.8c87defc60de": "The left pane is this wiki's existing heuristic simulator: a hand-tuned animation that approximates a driving model's feel from community sentiment text on a synthetic test loop (the Gauntlet). It does not run any real model.",
-  "content.2dd82d115610": "The right pane replays a recorded openpilot drive. It decodes modelV2 messages from a real rlog/qlog file and renders them using a direct TypeScript port of openpilot's onroad rendering code. The path and lane lines are actual model output from a real road. The panes show different routes; this compares a heuristic simulation with actual model output, rather than matching frames."
+  "content.2dd82d115610": "The right pane replays a recorded openpilot drive. It decodes modelV2 messages from a real rlog/qlog file and renders them using a direct TypeScript port of openpilot's onroad rendering code. The path and lane lines are actual model output from a real road. The panes show different routes; this compares a heuristic simulation with actual model output, rather than matching frames.",
+  "content.dc0446683764": "CTMV2 was announced September 8, 2026. Requires comma four or comma 3X plus a Chestnut eGPU. The October 6 master sync (#2036) uses selector 20 and Chestnut v27, and names Cinque Terre Model v2 as the default big model. Dev and staging builds based on that sync are development builds; the latest tagged release remains v2026.002.002.",
+  "content.462278a5f825": "CTV3M is dated September 17, 2026 and requires selector 20. Master now consumes Chestnut v27, which includes V3, following the October 6 sync (#2036). Check your installed branch and compatible hardware; older selector-19 builds use different catalogs. No dedicated V3 forum poll was verified.",
+  "content.05d1bee225fd": "Cinque Terre and V2 have positive overall polls but mixed vehicle-specific reports. Check stopping, cornering, and low-speed steering on your setup. Master now includes V3 in Chestnut v27 with selector 20; no dedicated V3 forum poll was verified. Hardware and branch compatibility still apply.",
+  "content.8ef3d91fc217": "Choose a driving model and tune steer delay or turn desires for your setup. Master now uses selector 20 with Chestnut v27 and Qualcomm v23 after the October 6 sync (#2036). Qualcomm v24 adoption remains proposed in open PR #2044. Refresh Models was added by #2018; refresh while parked with no download in progress. Clear Cache removes downloaded models.",
+  "content.d39a7caece07": "Refresh action: https://github.com/sunnypilot/sunnypilot/pull/2018. Master moved to selector 20, Chestnut v27, and Qualcomm v23 through the October 6 sync: https://github.com/sunnypilot/sunnypilot/pull/2036. PR #2015 is still open, although selector 20 is already in master. Qualcomm v24 adoption is an open proposal: https://github.com/sunnypilot/sunnypilot/pull/2044.",
+  "content.d0a80a6226ce": "The wiki documents 130 models. The models available on your device depend on its hardware and installed branch.",
+  "content.5f84dae1dd80": "Browse 130 documented driving models with release dates and community evidence. Device availability depends on hardware and the installed branch.",
+  "content.070223c6ad0a": "These are the \"big models\" — chestnut-class networks larger than anything in the WMI or OP lines, tied to comma's new GPU add-on, which began reaching owners in August 2026. They drop under the forum's big_model tag on a near-daily cadence during a run. The extra network size shows up first in lateral: taking in-town 90-degree turns wide instead of cutting them, and showing planted rather than floaty highway stability. Standout entries like Cinque Terre and Sad Model have significantly improved lateral stability and natural steering feel, while earlier BMRLNAP runs suffered from low-speed steering oscillations. Stop signs and traffic light stop lines remain an active area of tuning across the line. Runtime notes (October 2): PR #2035 proposes 1344×760 comma 3X frames before unified AMD transfer. PR #2023 proposes ChestnutPowerLimit (0 = stock; 40–100 W) via advanced sunnylink Device controls on comma four. Both remain open. Model management (October 9): the October 6 sync (#2036) moved master to selector 20, Chestnut v27, and Qualcomm v23. Qualcomm v24 is published, but its adoption is proposed in open PR #2044. PR #2015 remains open; selector 20 is already in master through the sync. PR #1999 proposes diagnosing stale compiled-runtime startup failures that can appear as Posenet NaN-speed alerts."
 }
